1
00:00:00,299 --> 00:00:02,329
(Penny:)No.
You'll wish it would kill you.

2
00:00:05,070 --> 00:00:06,140
(Amy:)So what do we do now?

3
00:00:06,138 --> 00:00:07,408
(Leonard:)They have
some board games.

4
00:00:07,406 --> 00:00:10,006
(Sheldon:)Eh, most of the Jenga
pieces are missing

5
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:12,038
(Sheldon:)and the Scrabble
only has seven tiles,

6
00:00:12,044 --> 00:00:14,544
(Sheldon:)so unless you want to build
an unimpressive structure

7
00:00:14,546 --> 00:00:17,546
with the word "SHNERPF"
next to it, move on.

8
00:00:17,549 --> 00:00:19,319
(Penny:)Hey, let's light a fire.

9
00:00:19,318 --> 00:00:21,448
(Amy:)Ooh, that sounds cozy.

10
00:00:21,453 --> 00:00:23,023
(Bernadette:)I don't think
I've lit a real fire before.

11
00:00:23,021 --> 00:00:24,851
(Sheldon:)Ah, it's basic thermodynamics.

12
00:00:24,856 --> 00:00:26,256
(Sheldon:)I'm sure we can figure that out.

13
00:00:26,258 --> 00:00:29,558
(Leonard:)I could stack the logs conically
to facilitate airflow.

14
00:00:29,561 --> 00:00:32,161
(Sheldon:)That would maximize oxygen
for optimal combustion.

15
00:00:32,164 --> 00:00:33,634
(fire whooshes)
Right. So all we need is to...

16
00:00:33,632 --> 00:00:35,202
(Penny:)Got it.

17
00:00:37,502 --> 00:00:39,472
(Leonard:)A scientist made that.

18
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:45,410
(Howard:)Look, Raj, you're my
best friend in the world

19
00:00:45,410 --> 00:00:50,110
(Howard:)and I really appreciate
your enthusiasm about the baby.

20
00:00:50,115 --> 00:00:52,945
(Raj:)Please, my pleasure.

21
00:00:54,353 --> 00:00:55,553
(Bernadette:)And, of course,
Howie and I

22
00:00:55,554 --> 00:00:57,154
(Bernadette:)both want you to be
a part of all this.

23
00:00:57,155 --> 00:01:00,225
(Howard:)But we have to set
some boundaries.

